    "slug": "somali-deputy-pm-discusses-agricultural-cooperation-with-ifad",
    "summary": "Somalia's Deputy Prime Minister Salah Ahmed Jama met with IFAD's regional director Naoufel Telahigue in Mogadishu to strengthen cooperation on agriculture, livestock, food security and climate resilience.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, 29 August 2026 — Somalia's Deputy Prime Minister Salah Ahmed Jama hosted the regional director of the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD) in the capital on Saturday, a meeting focused on deepening bilateral ties and advancing rural development.\n\nThe visiting official, Naoufel Telahigue, oversees IFAD operations across the Middle East, North Africa, Europe and Central Asia. Their discussions centered on joint efforts to modernize agriculture and livestock sectors, improve food availability, and help local communities adapt to the effects of climate change. Both sides also addressed ways to support smallholder farmers through better access to inputs and training.\n\nThe meeting comes as Somalia faces recurring droughts and rising food insecurity, challenges that disproportionately affect rural livelihoods. IFAD has a long history of financing agricultural development projects in the country, and this exchange signals a renewed commitment to scaling up those efforts.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom invest in farming and livestock businesses back home, this partnership could translate into more resilient supply chains and greater employment opportunities. Enhanced cooperation may also open doors for diaspora-led ventures that align with national agricultural priorities.\n\nNo formal agreements were announced following the talks, but both officials described the discussion as constructive and expressed optimism about future collaboration on sustainable farming and climate-adaptive practices.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/29/soomaaliya-iyo-ifad-oo-xoojinaya-iskaashiga-horumarinta-beeraha/",
